E["npc:chronormu"] = {t="npc",n="Chronormu",z="westernplaguelands",s="In the Western Plaguelands, Chronormu works to mend time's damaged threads. Mortals know her as Chromie, a bronze dragon who often works beside them.",h="In the Western Plaguelands, Chronormu works to mend time's damaged threads.",sec={{t="A Dragon in Small Guise",b="Mortals know Chronormu as Chromie, an eccentric and cheerful female gnome. She belongs to the bronze dragonflight and serves Nozdormu, the Timeless One. The titans charged bronze dragons to guard history and correct disruptions in the timeways. In her gnome form, Chronormu walks among mortals as an approachable and optimistic peer.",sp=0},{t="Watcher of the Plaguelands",b="Among Lordaeron's ruined remains, Chronormu watches over the devastated Western Plaguelands. The kingdom's fall and the Scourge's spread tore at the region's history, leaving temporal anomalies and trapped remnants. From places such as the ruins of Andorhal, she works quietly with mortal adventurers to mend tangled timelines and investigate disturbances. Only when necessary does she reveal the full majesty of the dragonflight.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Is Chromie really a gnome?",a="No. Chromie is Chronormu's mortal guise; she is a bronze dragon. Bronze dragons take mortal forms to walk among younger races without causing undue fear or suspicion.",al={"is chromie a gnome","chromie true form","who is chromie"}},{q="Why does Chromie have two names?",a="Chronormu is her true name as a bronze dragon. Among mortals, she uses the shorter name Chromie in her gnome guise.",al={"chronormu name gender","why is chromie called chronormu","chronormu gender"}},{q="What is Chromie doing in the Western Plaguelands?",a="The Scourge's devastation of Lordaeron disrupted history and the timeways. From the ruins, Chromie investigates temporal anomalies, undoes historical disturbances, and enlists trustworthy adventurers to repair damaged threads of time.",al={"what is chromie doing here","why is chromie in andorhal","chromie western plaguelands"}},{q="Who are the bronze dragonflight?",a="Led by Nozdormu, the Dragon Aspect, the bronze dragonflight was blessed by the titans with power over time's pathways. Its members protect those pathways and intervene when time is altered or corrupted, so history unfolds as intended.",al={"bronze dragons","what is bronze flight","nozdormu flight"}}},ang={["race:Gnome"]="As a gnome, you may meet Chronormu as Chromie, a cheerful figure whose small form hides a bronze dragon.",["class:Mage"]="As a mage studying chronomancy, you may find Chronormu's casual command of time and localized temporal pockets fascinating, and staggering in scale."},kw={"andorhal","bronze dragon","chromie","chronormu","nozdormu","visage"},rel={"zone:westernplaguelands","topic:gnome"},src={"Chronormu"}}
E["npc:darkmaster-gandling"] = {t="npc",n="Darkmaster Gandling",z="westernplaguelands",s="Beneath Caer Darrow, Darkmaster Gandling trains necromancers for the Scourge. From Scholomance, he serves the Cult of the Damned through experiments on the living and the dead.",h="Beneath Caer Darrow, Darkmaster Gandling trains necromancers for the Scourge.",sec={{t="The Headmaster's Domain",b="Darkmaster Gandling rules Scholomance beneath Caer Darrow. The academy trains aspiring necromancers for the Scourge. Gandling is a living human of the Cult of the Damned. With the lich Ras Frostwhisper, he committed atrocities against innocent captives taken from the surrounding lands. In the classrooms, students learn to brew plagues, reanimate the dead, and sculpt flesh.",sp=0},{t="Master of the Reliquary",b="In the Headmaster's Study, Gandling commands Scholomance's dark relics and trapped spirits. He joins arcane and shadow magic with forbidden necromancy. With these arts, he curses intruders and hurls them through shadow portals into sealed chambers around the study. There, they face the risen dead alone while Gandling shields himself from harm.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Darkmaster Gandling?",a="Darkmaster Gandling runs Scholomance, where he trains necromancers to serve the Lich King. He is a human of the Cult of the Damned.",al={"who is gandling","darkmaster gandling lore","scholomance boss"}},{q="Is Gandling an undead or a living human?",a="Gandling is a living human mortal, though he commands death magic and serves the Scourge. He leads mortal acolytes and cultists within Scholomance.",al={"is gandling undead","is gandling alive","gandling race"}},{q="What is his connection to Ras Frostwhisper?",a="Ras Frostwhisper taught Gandling. The human headmaster and the powerful lich presided over Scholomance's dark instruction and oversaw horrors against innocent souls such as the Sarkhoffs within Caer Darrow.",al={"frostwhisper gandling","ras frostwhisper teacher"}},{q="Where is Darkmaster Gandling found?",a="Gandling resides in the Headmaster's Study at the bottom of Scholomance. The catacombs beneath Caer Darrow in Darrowmere Lake lead to it.",al={"gandling location","where is gandling","how to find gandling"}}},ang={["class:Mage"]="As a Mage, you may see Gandling twisting Dalaran's scholarly traditions toward the making of undeath.",["race:Undead"]="As an Undead, you may see Gandling as a hated overseer of Scourge indoctrination. Beneath Caer Darrow, he binds free souls into eternal enslavement."},kw={"caer darrow","cult of the damned","darkmaster gandling","gandling","headmaster","necromancer","scholomance"},rel={"subzone:scholomance","zone:westernplaguelands","topic:cult-of-the-damned","topic:scourge"},src={"Darkmaster Gandling"}}
E["npc:eva-sarkhoff"] = {t="npc",n="Eva Sarkhoff",z="westernplaguelands",s="Outside Scholomance, Eva Sarkhoff lingers with Lucien, her husband, and seeks vengeance for their deaths. Once head maid to House Barov, she asks mortals to destroy their cursed remains.",h="Outside Scholomance, Eva Sarkhoff lingers with Lucien, her husband, and seeks vengeance for their deaths.",sec={{t="The Fall of House Barov",b="For decades, Eva served as head maid to the wealthy Barov family at Caer Darrow. Her husband Lucien was the family butler. As the Barovs feared age and the loss of their vast wealth, they made a disastrous pact with Kel'Thuzad. They gradually gave their manor to the young Cult of the Damned, which turned it into Scholomance, a hidden school of necromancy.\n\nEva and Lucien hid in the keep's corridors for six months. They scavenged food as cultists and monstrosities took over their home.",sp=0},{t="The Butcher's Scalpel",b="The Scourge found Eva and Lucien, then delivered them to Doctor Theolen Krastinov, known as the Butcher. For weeks, Krastinov tortured them with experiments. Dark magic kept them alive beyond mortal endurance.\n\nAfter they died, ghouls fed on their corpses. Their restless spirits remained bound to Caer Darrow. Eva now begs travelers to slay Krastinov and burn their remains.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who was Eva Sarkhoff before she died?",a="For decades, Eva served as head maid to the noble Barov family at Caer Darrow. Her husband Lucien was the family butler.",al={"eva sarkhoff backstory","who is eva sarkhoff","eva lore"}},{q="How did Eva die?",a="After months hiding from the Cult of the Damned, Eva and Lucien were found and handed to Doctor Theolen Krastinov. He tortured them for weeks, using dark magic to keep them alive until they died. Ghouls then fed on their corpses.",al={"how did eva sarkhoff die","eva sarkhoff death","who killed eva"}},{q="Why is Eva's ghost still in Caer Darrow?",a="Eva's spirit remains bound to Caer Darrow after her torment. She cannot pass on until Doctor Krastinov is slain and her remains inside Scholomance are burned.",al={"why is eva a ghost","eva spirit","why is eva lingering"}}},ang={["class:Priest"]="As a priest, you see the cruelty of the Scourge in Eva and Lucien's torment. Their restless souls call for holy hands to grant them peace and cleanse the foul magic binding them.",["race:Human"]="As a human, you see Eva and her husband among Lordaeron's ordinary servants. Their corrupt aristocracy betrayed them when House Barov sold Caer Darrow to Kel'Thuzad."},kw={"barov","caer darrow","cult of the damned","eva sarkhoff","krastinov","lucien sarkhoff","scholomance","the butcher"},rel={"subzone:caer-darrow","subzone:scholomance","topic:cult-of-the-damned","topic:scourge","zone:westernplaguelands","quest:1066"},src={"Eva Sarkhoff"}}
E["subzone:andorhal"] = {t="subzone",n="Andorhal",z="westernplaguelands",s="In Andorhal, the Scourge still holds the ruined town. Once northern Lordaeron's thriving agricultural heart, it became the place where Kel'Thuzad tainted the grain with the Plague of Undeath. During the Third War, that harvest carried horror across the region.",h="In Andorhal, the Scourge still holds the ruined town.",sec={{t="Ground Zero of the Plague",b="Before the Third War, Andorhal gathered grain from across Lordaeron and sent it east to Hearthglen and Stratholme. As the Eastweald's prosperous granary, it fed a vast network. Kel'Thuzad and the Cult of the Damned chose the town to begin their plot. They tainted crates of grain with the Plague of Undeath, turning the kingdom's breadbasket into a source of sickness. Countless citizens were infected before the Crown understood the danger.",sp=0},{t="The Fall of the Silver Hand",b="Prince Arthas Menethil and Jaina Proudmoore first faced Kel'Thuzad in Andorhal and slew him. His death did not end the danger. After returning from Northrend as a champion of the Scourge, Arthas marched back to claim Kel'Thuzad's remains.\n\nUther the Lightbringer and the remaining Silver Hand paladins made a desperate stand to defend King Terenas's ashes. The paladins fell, and Arthas slew Uther, his former pupil. Now the once grand settlement is a blight-choked Scourge stronghold.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why is Andorhal so important to the plague's history?",a="Andorhal gathered and distributed grain across northern Lordaeron. Kel'Thuzad used its network to spread the Plague of Undeath through the harvest, sending tainted grain along the King's Road to Stratholme and nearby towns.",al={"how did plague start here","andorhal grain plague","why andorhal mattered"}},{q="Who controls Andorhal right now?",a="The Scourge holds Andorhal's ruins. Skeletal sentries, necromancers, and ghouls patrol its scorched streets, guarding the place where their victory began in the Western Plaguelands.",al={"who rules andorhal","scourge in andorhal","who is in charge of andorhal"}},{q="Did Uther the Lightbringer die here?",a="Yes. After Capital City fell, Uther and his paladins guarded the urn holding King Terenas's ashes on Andorhal's outskirts. Arthas attacked to seize it for Kel'Thuzad's remains, then dueled and slew his mentor on the road.",al={"where did uther die","uther death andorhal","did arthas kill uther here"}}},ang={["class:Paladin"]="As a paladin, you walk ground marked by the Silver Hand's blood. Uther the Lightbringer and his loyal knights made their final stand against Arthas here.",["race:Undead"]="As one of the Forsaken, you can see Andorhal's fields as a bitter reminder of your origins. The Cult of the Damned began the fall of your mortal lives here."},kw={"andorhal","grain","granary","kel'thuzad","plaguelands","scourge","uther"},rel={"zone:westernplaguelands","topic:scourge","topic:plague-of-undeath","topic:cult-of-the-damned","topic:arthas-menethil","subzone:stratholme","subzone:hearthglen","topic:lordaeron"},src={"Andorhal"}}
E["subzone:bulwark"] = {t="subzone",n="Bulwark",z="westernplaguelands",s="At Tirisfal's edge, Bulwark keeps watch over the Western Plaguelands. Forsaken and Argent Dawn forces hold the outpost together, and Horde expeditions set out from there into the tainted east.",h="At Tirisfal's edge, Bulwark keeps watch over the Western Plaguelands.",sec={{t="A Shield Against the Scourge",b="Forsaken guards hold Bulwark's palisade where Tirisfal Glades meets the Western Plaguelands. The outpost bars the road from blighted lands where the undead roam. Here, Forsaken forces work with the neutral Argent Dawn. Together, they call on seasoned Horde champions to strike at the Scourge and keep the Lich King's minions from reaching Tirisfal.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the purpose of the Bulwark?",a="Bulwark is the Horde's forward defense against the Scourge and a base for its forces. It guards Tirisfal Glades and the Undercity from attacks out of the Western Plaguelands. Argent Dawn and Forsaken commanders coordinate strikes into the blighted lands.",al={"why is bulwark here","purpose of bulwark","what is this place"},it="purpose"},{q="Can Alliance characters visit the Bulwark to speak with the Argent Dawn?",a="No. The Argent Dawn representatives at Bulwark are neutral, but Forsaken guards garrison the encampment. Alliance visitors who enter the palisade are attacked on sight.",al={"can alliance use bulwark","alliance at bulwark","is bulwark horde only"},gp=true},{q="Is the Bulwark safe for young adventurers leaving Tirisfal?",a="No. The gate opens onto Tirisfal Glades, but the Western Plaguelands beyond hold deadly undead and plague cauldrons. Novice travelers who pass the palisade face swift death.",al={"can low levels go past bulwark","entering plaguelands low level"},it="danger"},{q="What is the Bulwark?",a="The Bulwark is a fortified outpost standing on the border between Tirisfal Glades and the Western Plaguelands. It serves as the Forsaken's eastern defensive line, guarding the entrance to Tirisfal against the unrelenting horrors of the Scourge. Here, Forsaken sentries and emissaries of the Argent Dawn work side by side to coordinate defense, hold back undead incursions, and dispatch capable champions into the blighted lands beyond.",al={"what is bulwark","the bulwark overview","about the bulwark"},it="place",add="3800d924"},{q="Who occupies the Bulwark?",a="The outpost is manned by Forsaken soldiers pledged to Queen Sylvanas alongside members of the neutral Argent Dawn. While the Forsaken guard the border and secure their northern kingdom, the Argent Dawn maintains a presence here to recruit experienced adventurers from the Horde, supplying them with missions to strike against the Lich King's minions across the Plaguelands.",al={"who runs bulwark","who is at the bulwark","bulwark residents"},it="residents",add="7098c368"},{q="Why is it called the Bulwark?",a="The fortification takes its name from its role as a literal bulwark—a defensive rampart built to protect the Forsaken lands from invasion. Standing squarely at the threshold where Tirisfal meets the Plaguelands, its heavy barricades form the final line of defense holding back the monstrous legions of the Scourge.",al={"why called bulwark","bulwark name meaning","why the name bulwark"},it="name",add="a92b042c"}},ang={["race:Undead"]="As Forsaken, you stand watch at Bulwark's narrow passage against the Lich King's armies. They must not march straight on Brill and the Undercity.",["faction:Horde"]="As Horde, you have Bulwark as your main gate and base for operations across the Plaguelands. The Alliance holds Chillwind Camp opposite."},kw={"argent dawn","bulwark","chillwind","forsaken","scourge","tirisfal","western plaguelands"},rel={"zone:westernplaguelands","zone:tirisfal","topic:forsaken","topic:argent-dawn","topic:scourge","subzone:chillwind-camp","topic:horde","topic:lordaeron"},src={"Bulwark"}}
E["subzone:caer-darrow"] = {t="subzone",n="Caer Darrow",z="westernplaguelands",s="Phantoms haunt Caer Darrow above Darrowmere Lake in the Western Plaguelands. House Barov once ruled from its keep, now sold to Kel'Thuzad and remade as Scholomance.",h="Phantoms haunt Caer Darrow above Darrowmere Lake in the Western Plaguelands.",sec={{t="A Legacy of War and Betrayal",b="Caer Darrow guarded Lordaeron and held an ancient elven runestone long before the Scourge. During the Second War, the Horde sacked the fortress and broke the stone apart for Gul'dan's Altars of Storms. Lord Uther the Lightbringer sailed to aid the survivors, but Alterac privateers ambushed his fleet. Their treachery exposed Alterac's betrayal to the Alliance.",sp=0},{t="The Fall of House Barov",b="After the Second War, Caer Darrow rose again as the Barov family's grand estate. Their vast land deeds reached across Brill, Tarren Mill, and Southshore. When age threatened their wealth and mortality, the Barovs bargained with Kel'Thuzad. The Cult of the Damned took root beneath the fortress and founded Scholomance.\n\nBefore the Third War swept across Lordaeron, a preliminary plague struck the island's servants and townsfolk. They perished, doomed to haunt the ruined keep as lingering echoes.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What is Caer Darrow?",a="Caer Darrow rises as an island fortress in Darrowmere Lake, within the Western Plaguelands. Once the ancestral manor of the wealthy Barov family, it is now a ruin above Scholomance's catacombs, a necromantic academy.",al={"caer darrow overview","what is this place","caer darrow lore"}},{q="Why is the town abandoned and ruined?",a="Caer Darrow was abandoned after the Barov family bargained with Kel'Thuzad and gave their estate to the Cult of the Damned in exchange for immortality. The cult loosed a fatal plague upon the settlement before Lordaeron's wider invasion began.",al={"why is caer darrow destroyed","what happened to caer darrow","caer darrow history"}},{q="Why can't I see the ghosts in the town?",a="The murdered inhabitants of Caer Darrow linger as restless spirits, caught in their final moments. Ordinary eyes cannot see them without special magical sight, such as the Spectral Essence provided by the spirits of Eva and Lucien Sarkhoff.",al={"where are the ghosts","invisible people caer darrow","how to see ghosts"},sp=1},{q="What was the runestone that used to be here?",a="During the Second War, Caer Darrow held an ancient high elven runestone. The Horde raided the island and chiseled the sacred stone into pieces. Gul'dan used them to build the Altars of Storms and channel magic into ogre mages.",al={"runestone at caer darrow","elven runestone","altar of storms stone"}},{q="What is underneath the fortress?",a="Scholomance lies beneath the keep as the Cult of the Damned's headquarters and training academy. Led by Darkmaster Gandling, its necromancers and acolytes study the dark arts and experiment on the dead.",al={"what is under caer darrow","what is in the basement","dungeon under caer darrow"}}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="For the Alliance, Caer Darrow recalls two betrayals. Alterac privateers ambushed Lord Uther the Lightbringer's fleet during the Second War, exposing King Perenolde's treason. Later, House Barov sold its ancestral home to Kel'Thuzad.",["race:Human"]="As a human, you can recognize Caer Darrow as the former seat of House Barov, once among Lordaeron's wealthiest noble families. Their greed led them to make pacts with the Cult of the Damned."},kw={"barov","caer darrow","cult of the damned","darrowmere lake","gandling","runestone","sarkhoff","scholomance","spectral essence"},rel={"subzone:scholomance","subzone:darrowmere-lake","zone:westernplaguelands","npc:eva-sarkhoff","topic:cult-of-the-damned","topic:alterac-kingdom","topic:second-war","npc:darkmaster-gandling"},src={"Caer Darrow"}}
E["subzone:chillwind-camp"] = {t="subzone",n="Chillwind Camp",z="westernplaguelands",s="At the southern pass, Chillwind Camp holds the Alliance line against the Scourge. Alliance soldiers and the Argent Dawn strike nearby strongholds and plague cauldrons from this outpost, before the blighted ruins of Lordaeron.",h="At the southern pass, Chillwind Camp holds the Alliance line against the Scourge.",sec={{t="The Edge of the Blight",b="Chillwind Camp guards the pass from Chillwind Point into the Western Plaguelands. It is the Alliance's first line of defense and its main base for pressing into the region. High mountain ridges keep the worst corruption at a distance, though the north's dead chill hangs over the tents and palisades.\n\nCommander Ashlam Valorfist leads a small garrison of soldiers, scouts, and Argent Dawn specialists. They contain horrors along the King's Road and gather intelligence to reclaim Lordaeron's fallen fields.",sp=0},{t="A War of Attrition",b="Without armies to assault Andorhal or Scholomance, Chillwind Camp depends on independent champions and mercenaries. Its forces strike the Cult of the Damned, disable plague cauldrons poisoning the soil, and keep supply routes open to eastern outposts such as Light's Hope Chapel. Scourge-held ruins lie just north, while the Forsaken fortify the western border. The defenders fight to keep the pass from being overwhelmed.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the purpose of Chillwind Camp?",a="Chillwind Camp is the Alliance and Argent Dawn's southern foothold on the Western Plaguelands' border. It is a secure base for attacks against the Scourge in Andorhal and efforts to disable the region's plague cauldrons.",al={"why is chillwind camp here","purpose of chillwind","what is chillwind camp"}},{q="How do you reach Chillwind Camp from Southshore?",a="From Southshore in the Hillsbrad Foothills, head north toward Tarren Mill, then follow the mountain trail into the far eastern Alterac Mountains. The path passes the troll ruins of Chillwind Point before descending north through a ravine into the camp.",al={"how to get to chillwind camp","directions to chillwind","path to chillwind"}},{q="What is the Horde equivalent of this outpost?",a="The Horde's counterpart is the Bulwark, on the western frontier between Tirisfal Glades and the Western Plaguelands. Both outposts are fortified bases for campaigns against the region's Scourge.",al={"horde chillwind camp","horde version of chillwind","is there a horde chillwind"}},{q="Who commands the forces at Chillwind Camp?",a="Commander Ashlam Valorfist leads the garrison at Chillwind Camp. He coordinates Alliance volunteers, Knights of the Silver Hand, and Argent Dawn liaisons in operations across nearby ruins and tainted farms.",al={"chillwind camp leader","who is in charge of chillwind camp","commander of chillwind"}}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance member, you can find safe refuge at Chillwind Camp. Griffons provide transit, and commanders issue orders for the effort against the Scourge in northern Lordaeron.",["class:Paladin"]="As a promising paladin, you receive direction from Lord Grayson Shadowbreaker in Stormwind to aid Commander Valorfist at Chillwind Camp. There, you bring the Silver Hand's holy wrath against the undead ranks."},kw={"alterac mountains","andorhal","argent dawn","ashlam valorfist","cauldrons","chillwind camp","chillwind point","western plaguelands"},rel={"zone:westernplaguelands","subzone:chillwind-point","subzone:andorhal","subzone:bulwark","subzone:scholomance","subzone:light-s-hope-chapel","topic:argent-dawn","npc:lord-grayson-shadowbreaker"},src={"Chillwind Camp"}}
E["subzone:dalson-s-tears"] = {t="subzone",n="Dalson's Tears",z="westernplaguelands",s="At Dalson's Tears, a Scourge cauldron poisons the fields of the Western Plaguelands. Once Dalson's Orchard, this farm became a Scourge staging ground during the Third War. Its former owners still haunt the fields and outbuildings.",h="At Dalson's Tears, a Scourge cauldron poisons the fields of the Western Plaguelands.",sec={{t="A Poisoned Harvest",b="Dalson's Tears was once Dalson's Orchard, a productive farm in Lordaeron's breadbasket. Decay now chokes the fields, while a great iron cauldron at their center sends green plague vapors across the land. Cauldron Lord Malvinious oversees it. Blighted zombies, rotting cadavers, and skeletal horrors guard the device in the Lich King's service.",sp=0},{t="The Fate of the Dalsons",b="The Dalson family fell to the plague, and death brought them no release. Mrs. Dalson, Farmer Dalson's wife, wanders the poisoned soil as a mindless skeleton with the key to the farm's outhouse. Inside the locked shack waits the ghoul who was once Farmer Dalson. His desperate wife locked him away before both fell to the Scourge's curse.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What was Dalson's Tears called before the plague?",a="Before the plague, the farm was called Dalson's Orchard, a prosperous plot in Lordaeron. The Third War devastated the land.",al={"dalson's orchard","original name","what was this farm called"}},{q="Why is there a giant cauldron in the middle of the farm?",a="The Scourge built great plague cauldrons across Lordaeron's farmland to boil toxins without pause. Their vapors drift across the region, blighting earth, poisoning water supplies, and corrupting living creatures exposed to them.",al={"dalson cauldron","green smoke kettle","why is there a cauldron here"}},{q="Who guards the cauldron at Dalson's Tears?",a="Cauldron Lord Malvinious protects the plague cauldron. The Scourge serves him, with blighted zombies, skeletal terrors, and rotting cadavers at his side.",al={"cauldron lord","who is the boss here","cauldron lord malvinious"}},{q="What is known about the locked outhouse?",a="The locked outhouse is part of the abandoned farm. Mrs. Dalson's diary offers clues to the family's fate.",al={"outhouse monster","who is in the outhouse","farmer dalson"},sp=1}},ang={["race:Undead"]="For the Forsaken, this ruined homestead recalls the fate of many people of Lordaeron. Sylvanas Windrunner broke the Lich King's control over them.",["class:Paladin"]="As a paladin, you can see the lingering evil in the desecrated fields and the suffering souls of the Dalson family. The Light's holy warriors are sworn to cleanse that evil from Lordaeron."},kw={"cauldron lord malvinious","dalson's orchard","dalson's tears","farmer dalson","mrs dalson","plague cauldron","western plaguelands"},rel={"zone:westernplaguelands","topic:scourge","topic:lich-king"},src={"Dalson's Tears"}}
E["subzone:darrowmere-lake"] = {t="subzone",n="Darrowmere Lake",z="westernplaguelands",s="At the heart of the Western Plaguelands, Darrowmere Lake surrounds Caer Darrow. The island fortress holds ruined halls above Scholomance, the Cult of the Damned's academy of necromancy.",h="At the heart of the Western Plaguelands, Darrowmere Lake surrounds Caer Darrow.",sec={{t="A Storied Inland Sea",b="Darrowmere Lake is among the largest inland waters in the Eastern Kingdoms. The Thondroril and Darrowmere rivers feed its deep waters, beneath the blighted forests of Lordaeron. During the Second War, the Horde and Grand Admiral Daelin Proudmoore's fleet fought naval skirmishes here.\n\nThe Horde sacked Caer Darrow on the central island and carried away its ancient runestone. Once, the thriving House of Barov sent trade across the lake. Now a grim basin lies veiled in mist at the heart of the Plaguelands.",sp=0},{t="The Shadow on the Waters",b="Caer Darrow rises from the center of Darrowmere Lake. It was once the proud ancestral seat of the Barov family. Beneath its broken foundations lies Scholomance, the Scourge's chief academy of necromancy and dark arts. The waters around the island are stagnant, reflecting the Cult of the Damned's dark legacy. To reach the fortress at the lake's heart, you must cross those waters through the dangers of the blighted countryside.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where is Darrowmere Lake located?",a="Darrowmere Lake lies in the southeastern corner of the Western Plaguelands. It joins the Thondroril River to the north with the Darrowmere River flowing south.",al={"darrowmere location","where is darrowmere lake","how to get to darrowmere"}},{q="What is on the island in the center of the lake?",a="Caer Darrow, an ancient settlement once ruled by the noble House of Barov, occupies the island. Beneath the ruined town lies Scholomance, a sprawling school of dark magic run by the Cult of the Damned.",al={"island in darrowmere","what is on the island","caer darrow location"}},{q="What role did Darrowmere Lake play in the Second War?",a="During the Second War, Darrowmere Lake was a contested waterway. The Proudmoore fleet fought naval battles against the Horde, which also sacked Caer Darrow and seized its ancient runestone.",al={"second war darrowmere","naval battles darrowmere","darrowmere history"}},{q="Can ships still sail into Darrowmere Lake?",a="Large vessels can no longer reach Darrowmere Lake from the sea. The connecting rivers have steep waterfalls and shallow passages, though massive fleets sailed the lake during the Second War.",al={"darrowmere boat access","can ships reach darrowmere"}}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="For Alliance veterans, Darrowmere Lake recalls a key naval front. Proudmoore's fleet fought the Old Horde here during the Second War.",["race:Undead"]="As an undead, you know Darrowmere Lake marks the threshold of Caer Darrow. There, the living Barovs bargained away their mortal home to the Lich King to create Scholomance, the dread academy."},kw={"barov","caer darrow","darrowmere","darrowmere lake","proudmoore fleet","scholomance","thondroril river","western plaguelands"},rel={"zone:westernplaguelands","subzone:caer-darrow","subzone:scholomance","subzone:thondroril-river","topic:cult-of-the-damned","topic:lordaeron","topic:second-war","subzone:stratholme"},src={"Darrowmere Lake"}}
E["subzone:felstone-field"] = {t="subzone",n="Felstone Field",z="westernplaguelands",s="Scourge corruption has claimed Felstone Field in the northwestern Western Plaguelands. Once farmland for Lordaeron, it now lies in ruins beneath a plague cauldron that sends toxic fumes into the air.",h="Scourge corruption has claimed Felstone Field in the northwestern Western Plaguelands.",sec={{t="A Blighted Homestead",b="Felstone Field once fed Lordaeron from a peaceful family farm. When plague swept through the north, the Cult of the Damned and the Scourge quickly seized the homestead. Dead weeds and rot cover the fields now. At the farm’s heart, an enormous plague cauldron churns foul vapors into the sky. Cauldron Lord Bilemaw guards it with skeletal flayers, sorcerers, and ravenous ghouls.",sp=0},{t="Lingering Ghosts and Zealots",b="Traces of the living world remain among the ruins. In the northeastern farmhouse, Janice Felstone’s ghost wanders the shell of her former home in sorrow. Scarlet Crusade patrols prowl the property’s borders. They violently purge any undead they find and strike down outsiders who venture too close to their crusade.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What is the cauldron in the center of the field doing?",a="The cauldron is a Scourge plague engine that spreads pestilence through the surrounding land and air. It corrupts the soil and raises the dead. Cauldron Lord Bilemaw guards it with skeletal minions and ghouls.",al={"felstone cauldron","why is there a cauldron","plague cauldron felstone"}},{q="Who is the ghost inside the farmhouse?",a="The ghost is Janice Felstone, the farmstead’s former mistress. She died when the Scourge overran the territory, and her spirit remains tied to her family’s house, unwilling or unable to rest.",al={"janice felstone","ghost in felstone house","who is in the house"}},{q="Why are there Scarlet Crusaders patrolling the farm?",a="The Scarlet Crusade sends aggressive strike teams into the Western Plaguelands to destroy the Scourge. They treat Horde and Alliance travelers who trespass as possible plague-bearers or enemies, and attack them on sight.",al={"scarlet crusade felstone","crusaders at felstone field"}},{q="Who actually owns the deed to Felstone Field?",a="Jeremiah Payson in the Undercity and Ol' Emma in Stormwind both claim their sister, Janice Felstone, gave them the deed. Whether two deeds were drawn up or the plague’s chaos tangled the inheritance between living and undead family members remains a mystery.",al={"felstone field deed","who owns felstone","better late than never deed"},sp=1}},ang={["race:Undead"]="As Forsaken, you can see in this ruined farm a reminder of the lives your people once led in Lordaeron. Relatives such as Jeremiah Payson survived only through undeath.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance survivor in Stormwind, you may see Felstone Field as lost ancestral land and displaced kin. Ol' Emma still claims a ruined inheritance in the north."},kw={"cauldron lord bilemaw","felstone field","janice felstone","jeremiah payson","lordaeron","ol' emma","plague cauldron","scarlet crusade","western plaguelands"},rel={"zone:westernplaguelands","topic:scourge","topic:alliance","topic:horde"},src={"Felstone Field"}}
E["subzone:gahrron-s-withering"] = {t="subzone",n="Gahrron's Withering",z="westernplaguelands",s="At Gahrron's Withering, the Scourge foul an old Lordaeron farm beside the road to the Eastern Plaguelands. A massive cauldron sends plague vapors into the air.",h="At Gahrron's Withering, the Scourge foul an old Lordaeron farm beside the road to the Eastern Plaguelands.",sec={{t="From Harvest to Decay",b="Before the Third War, this farm fed Lordaeron with grain. Then the Cult of the Damned and the Scourge swept across the land, and the fields fell silent. Now the farmstead is broken and derelict. Haunting visions, wailing wraiths, and restless spirits roam its ruined outbuildings under Scourge overseers sworn to the Lich King.",sp=0},{t="The Cauldron and the Fall of Redpath",b="Cauldron Lord Soulwrath tends a massive Scourge plague cauldron in the heart of the blighted fields. Noxious miasma pours from it, poisoning the earth and driving natural life away.\n\nThis farm also marks the tragic end of the nearby Darrowshire tragedy. Alliance defenders confronted Captain Joseph Redpath here and struck him down after dark corruption claimed him. His shattered shield remains in the cursed soil.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What was Gahrron's Withering called before the plague?",a="No record preserves the farm's name before the plague. Now it is known only as Gahrron's Withering. It was a working Lordaeron homestead until the Scourge devastated the countryside.",al={"original name","old name","gahrrons quickening"}},{q="Why is there a giant cauldron here?",a="The Scourge placed the cauldron here to spread plague vapors across the region. Cauldron Lord Soulwrath guards it so it can keep blighting the soil and air.",al={"plague cauldron","what does the cauldron do","pot in field"}},{q="Who was Joseph Redpath and why does he matter here?",a="Captain Joseph Redpath defended nearby Darrowshire and is named among the town's heroes. His cracked shield lies near the farmstead's barn, a relic of Darrowshire's tragic fall.",al={"redpath shield","captain redpath","darrowshire connection"},sp=1},{q="Who controls Gahrron's Withering right now?",a="The Scourge holds the farm. Spectral wraiths, wailing deaths, and haunting visions haunt it under Cauldron Lord Soulwrath, a powerful necromantic officer.",al={"who is here","mobs at gahrron","scourge in charge"}}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="For Alliance veterans, this farm carries a grim memory. Captain Joseph Redpath's cracked shield remains in the cursed soil, left from Darrowshire's fall.",["class:Paladin"]="As a paladin, you find a clear target in the vile fumes from Cauldron Lord Soulwrath's cauldron and the restless dead on the ruined fields."},kw={"cauldron","darrowshire","gahrron","gahrron's withering","joseph redpath","soulwrath"},rel={"subzone:cauldron","subzone:darrowshire","subzone:chillwind-camp","zone:westernplaguelands","topic:scourge","topic:argent-dawn","topic:alliance","topic:lich-king"},src={"Gahrron's Withering"}}
E["subzone:hearthglen"] = {t="subzone",n="Hearthglen",z="westernplaguelands",s="In the northern hills of the Western Plaguelands, Hearthglen holds firm. Its walls survived Lordaeron's fall, and the Scarlet Crusade now uses the settlement and its farmlands as a northern stronghold and training ground.",h="In the northern hills of the Western Plaguelands, Hearthglen holds firm.",sec={{t="A Bastion in the Blight",b="Hearthglen still looks like a living town of Lordaeron, while nearby Andorhal lies in skeletal ruin. Its lumber mill, scout towers, stables, and working mine are still here. Lord Tirion Fordring once governed from Mardenholde Keep. During the Second War, Hearthglen prospered and stood staunchly defended.\n\nWhen the Plague of Undeath swept Lordaeron during the Third War, Prince Arthas Menethil intercepted tainted grain here. He purged the infected townsfolk and joined Uther the Lightbringer to repel a massive Scourge siege. Hearthglen's formidable walls survived intact.",sp=0},{t="Under the Scarlet Banner",b="After the kingdom's collapse, the Silver Hand fell into disarray. Tirion's son, Taelan Fordring, renounced the order and joined the Scarlet Crusade. Grief and zealotry soon consumed the fortress. Scarlet crusaders now patrol Hearthglen's approaches and man its ramparts. They execute any outsider, living or undead, who trespasses on their land.\n\nHighlord Taelan Fordring rules from Mardenholde Keep. From there, he serves the Crusade's uncompromising war against the Plaguelands.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why does Hearthglen look so clean compared to the rest of the Plaguelands?",a="Prince Arthas and Uther the Lightbringer helped spare Hearthglen from utter ruin during the Third War. They slew early plague victims and broke a massive Scourge siege. Later, the Scarlet Crusade fortified the pass and valley, purging the encroaching Scourge before the rot could take hold.",al={"why is hearthglen intact","hearthglen not destroyed","hearthglen alive"}},{q="Who controls Hearthglen right now?",a="The Scarlet Crusade controls Hearthglen from Mardenholde Keep, where Highlord Taelan Fordring rules. He is the son of Tirion Fordring, the former lord and famed paladin.",al={"who rules hearthglen","hearthglen leader","who is in charge of hearthglen"}},{q="Is Hearthglen friendly to Alliance or Horde visitors?",a="No. The Scarlet Crusade treats all outsiders with extreme hostility and paranoia. They see Horde members as monstrous abominations. Unaligned Alliance travelers are condemned as plague-carriers or heretics and marked for execution on sight.",al={"can i go to hearthglen","is hearthglen hostile","hearthglen safe"}},{q="What happened to Tirion Fordring?",a="Years before the Third War, Tirion was stripped of his title and excommunicated by the Alliance for defending an honorable orc named Eitrigg. Exiled to the wilds, he left Hearthglen behind. Command of Mardenholde eventually passed to his son, Taelan.",al={"where is tirion","tirion hearthglen history","why isn't tirion here"}}},ang={["class:Paladin"]="As a paladin, you walk the approaches to a place once home to Tirion Fordring. His son now holds Hearthglen for the Scarlet Crusade. The town shows how tragically the order splintered into a fanatical crusade.",["race:Undead"]="As a Forsaken, you face a lethal thorn in the north at Hearthglen. Its crusaders hate the undead and patrol to eradicate any scouts venturing north from Andorhal."},kw={"andorhal","hearthglen","mardenholde","scarlet crusade","taelan fordring","tirion fordring","western plaguelands"},rel={"subzone:mardenholde-keep","zone:westernplaguelands","npc:tirion-fordring","topic:scarlet-crusade","subzone:andorhal","topic:arthas-menethil","topic:plague-of-undeath","npc:eitrigg"},src={"Hearthglen"}}
E["subzone:mardenholde-keep"] = {t="subzone",n="Mardenholde Keep",z="westernplaguelands",s="In western Lordaeron, the Scarlet Crusade holds Hearthglen from Mardenholde Keep. Highlord Taelan Fordring rules from the fortress once held by his father, Tirion.",h="In western Lordaeron, the Scarlet Crusade holds Hearthglen from Mardenholde Keep.",sec={{t="Seat of the Fordrings",b="Mardenholde Keep once governed the principality of Hearthglen and the vales around it. Lord Tirion Fordring ruled from its council chambers with trusted advisors, keeping peace across the region. For generations, Lordaeron's people praised the fortress because it never fell during the Second War.\n\nThen Tirion defended the orc Eitrigg and was exiled. Governance passed to his ambitious apprentice, Barthilas, and later to Tirion's son, Taelan. Taelan inherited his father's domain on the eve of Lordaeron's destruction.",sp=0},{t="Cradle of the Crusade",b="The Scourge advanced through Lordaeron, and Mardenholde Keep came beneath the Scarlet Crusade's banner. Paranoia and dark subversion soon took root in the Crusade's ranks. Dathrohan and the most fervent zealots held Hearthglen as a fortified stronghold for the Crusade.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who controls Mardenholde Keep right now?",a="The Scarlet Crusade controls Mardenholde Keep, its main military command in the Western Plaguelands. Highlord Taelan Fordring rules from the main hall, surrounded by elite Scarlet protectors.",al={"who leads mardenholde","who is in charge of hearthglen keep","mardenholde boss"}},{q="Why is this fortress so important to Tirion Fordring?",a="Mardenholde Keep was Tirion Fordring's ancestral home and the seat from which he ruled the region as an Alliance paladin. He raised his family there, then lost his titles and was exiled for defending an honorable enemy.",al={"tirion connection to mardenholde","did tirion live here"}},{q="How did the Scarlet Crusade take over Mardenholde?",a="After Tirion's exile and Lordaeron's fall during the Third War, his son Taelan renounced the Silver Hand and joined the Scarlet Crusade. The keep and its garrison now serve the Crusade.",al={"how did scarlet crusade get hearthglen","why is scarlet crusade here"}},{q="Can players enter Mardenholde Keep safely?",a="No. The Scarlet Crusade sees outsiders as possible plague carriers or enemies of its cause. Anyone who approaches the keep will be attacked unless protected by powerful illusion magic.",al={"is mardenholde friendly","can alliance enter mardenholde","can horde enter mardenholde"}}},ang={["class:Paladin"]="For a paladin, Mardenholde Keep marks a tragic chapter in the order's history. The Silver Hand's former sanctuary became a place where the order split between the fanatical Scarlet Crusade and the vigilant Argent Dawn.",["race:Human"]="As a human of Lordaeron, you may see Mardenholde Keep as a bitter reminder. Its proud strongholds survived the orcish wars, only to fall to madness and zealotry during the Scourge."},kw={"dathrohan","hearthglen","mardenholde","scarlet crusade","silver hand","taelan fordring","tirion fordring"},rel={"subzone:hearthglen","npc:tirion-fordring","topic:scarlet-crusade","topic:knights-of-the-silver-hand","topic:argent-dawn","zone:westernplaguelands","topic:lordaeron","npc:eitrigg"},src={"Mardenholde Keep"}}
E["subzone:northridge-lumber-camp"] = {t="subzone",n="Northridge Lumber Camp",z="westernplaguelands",s="Scarlet Crusade guards hold Northridge Lumber Camp, an active, fortified mill in the hills near Hearthglen. Its timber feeds nearby strongholds, and the Alliance and Horde seek ways to cripple the Crusade’s supply.",h="Scarlet Crusade guards hold Northridge Lumber Camp, an active, fortified mill in the hills near Hearthglen.",sec={{t="Fueling the Crusade",b="Scarlet Crusade workers fell and process timber at Northridge Lumber Camp, despite the plague in the surrounding forests. The mill lies down the road from Hearthglen, in the northern hills of the Western Plaguelands. Its wood builds fortifications, repairs watchtowers, and sustains the Crusade’s war effort in Lordaeron. Guards and laborers garrison the camp in force, defending it from the Scourge and trespassers.",sp=0},{t="Target for Sabotage",b="Hearthglen depends on Northridge Lumber Camp for timber to maintain its defenses. That need makes the mill a target for outside forces. Alliance commanders and Horde scouts know a direct assault on fortified Crusade positions would cost dearly. So their agents seek quieter ways to sabotage the operation, such as releasing wood-boring termites into the lumber stores and spoiling the Crusade’s supplies from within.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who controls Northridge Lumber Camp?",a="The Scarlet Crusade controls and operates Northridge Lumber Camp. Its guards and laborers harvest timber for nearby strongholds.",al={"who runs northridge","who controls the lumber mill","northridge faction"}},{q="Why is this lumber mill important?",a="The mill supplies timber for the Scarlet Crusade’s fortifications and watchtowers. That wood supports its nearby strongholds and war effort in Lordaeron.",al={"why does northridge matter","significance of northridge","what is this camp for"}},{q="Why do the Alliance and Horde want to sabotage it?",a="The Alliance and Horde see the aggressive, fanatical Scarlet Crusade as a threat in the Plaguelands. Sabotage can weaken its lumber supplies and defenses without the cost of a direct assault.",al={"why attack northridge","termites quest","why ruin the lumber"}},{q="Who ran the mill before the Third War?",a="Before the Kingdom of Lordaeron fell to the Scourge, local civilian families lived and worked at the mill. It was a quiet regional enterprise.",al={"who owned northridge lumber camp","history of northridge mill"}}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance scout, you face the Scarlet Crusade’s violent xenophobia during reconnaissance and operations in northern Lordaeron, though the Crusade claims to fight the undead.",["faction:Horde"]="As a Forsaken or Horde ally, you can weaken Hearthglen by disrupting the Crusade’s lumber supply and pressuring its zealots toward their strongholds."},kw={"hearthglen","levine","lumber","mill","northridge","plaguelands","scarlet crusade","termites"},rel={"subzone:hearthglen","topic:scarlet-crusade","zone:westernplaguelands","topic:alliance","topic:horde","topic:third-war"},src={"Northridge Lumber Camp"}}
E["subzone:plaguemist-ravine"] = {t="subzone",n="Plaguemist Ravine",z="westernplaguelands",s="In western Plaguelands, sickly fog drifts south through Plaguemist Ravine. The narrow passage links the Hinterlands to Darrowmere Lake and offers a quiet, desolate route across the range.",h="In western Plaguelands, sickly fog drifts south through Plaguemist Ravine.",sec={{t="A Blighted Threshold",b="Northwest of Quel'Danil Lodge, Plaguemist Ravine cuts between the Hinterlands and the Western Plaguelands. Lush, untamed highland forest lies to the south. Northward, the pass opens onto Caer Darrow and the blighted shores of Darrowmere Lake. The two realms could hardly be more different. Foul vapors creep south from the Plaguelands, meeting the crisp mountain air of the neighboring wilderness.",sp=0},{t="A Quiet Passage",b="Though the ravine cuts into Scourge-ravaged territory, it remains remarkably deserted. No wild beasts or wandering undead linger in the gorge. Its winding path makes a convenient, if ominous, back road for daring couriers and adventurers. They can use it to bypass the heavily fortified highways and border checkpoints leading into Lordaeron.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where does Plaguemist Ravine lead?",a="Plaguemist Ravine links the Hinterlands to the Western Plaguelands. Northward, it opens onto Darrowmere Lake's shores near the island fortress of Caer Darrow. Southward, it leads to forested hills northwest of Quel'Danil Lodge.",al={"where does plaguemist ravine go","plaguemist ravine path","plaguemist connection"}},{q="Why is it called Plaguemist Ravine?",a="Plaguemist Ravine takes its name from the pervasive, blighted fog drifting south from the Western Plaguelands. The sickly air sharply contrasts with the fresh, uncorrupted atmosphere of the Hinterlands.",al={"why is it called plaguemist","plaguemist name origin"}},{q="Are there any enemies or NPCs in the ravine?",a="No hostile creatures, wildlife, or friendly non-player characters linger in Plaguemist Ravine. It is an unusually quiet passage between two active zones.",al={"plaguemist ravine mobs","is plaguemist ravine safe"}},{q="How do you find the entrance in the Hinterlands?",a="In the Hinterlands, find the entrance in the northern mountain wall, west of Quel'Danil Lodge and north of Rhapsody Shindigger's campsite.",al={"how to find plaguemist ravine","plaguemist ravine entrance"}}},ang={["class:Hunter"]="As a hunter, you find a peaceful passage through the ravine. With no game or woodland beasts, it makes an eerie border as you track north into the Plaguelands.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance scout stationed at Quel'Danil Lodge, you can use the pass as a discreet route to watch the blighted shores around Caer Darrow without facing open road patrols."},kw={"caer darrow","darrowmere","hinterlands","mountain pass","plaguemist","plaguemist ravine","quel'danil","western plaguelands"},rel={"zone:westernplaguelands","zone:hinterlands","subzone:caer-darrow"},src={"Plaguemist Ravine"}}
E["subzone:ruins-of-andorhal"] = {t="subzone",n="Ruins of Andorhal",z="westernplaguelands",s="In the Western Plaguelands, Andorhal’s ruined streets belong to the Scourge. Once northern Lordaeron’s grain hub, the town now teems with undead abominations, ghouls, and wraiths under Araj the Summoner.",h="In the Western Plaguelands, Andorhal’s ruined streets belong to the Scourge.",sec={{t="Heart of the Plague",b="Andorhal packed the Cult of the Damned’s tainted grain and sent it across the human kingdom. That grain began Lordaeron’s plague of undeath. Now the ruined city is a Scourge stronghold in the Western Plaguelands. Araj the Summoner holds its center, surrounded by ghouls, skeletal horrors, and towering flesh golems. Scarlet Crusade scouting parties sometimes probe the outskirts, but the Scourge rules the shattered streets.",sp=0},{t="Unraveling Time",b="Strange disturbances in time trouble Andorhal alongside its undead host. The town hall clock and pocket watches scattered through the streets all stopped at three o’clock. Chromie, a bronze dragon, shelters in the inn at the ruins’ edge while she investigates temporal parasites nesting in the grain silos. Scourge forces seem to be tampering with time, hoping to alter the course of the city’s tragic fall.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who rules the Ruins of Andorhal?",a="Araj the Summoner rules the Ruins of Andorhal and directs Scourge activity there. The powerful lich dwells in the city center, guarded by skeletal warriors and flesh constructs.",al={"who leads andorhal","andorhal boss","araj the summoner"}},{q="Why is Chromie inside the ruins?",a="Chromie, disguised as a female gnome, investigates unnatural disturbances in time. She suspects something is happening around the city silos and asks travelers to help investigate.",al={"what is chromie doing in andorhal","why is chromie here","chromie andorhal"}},{q="Why are all the clocks stopped at three o'clock?",a="The town hall clock and personal watches found among the ruins stopped at three o’clock. They may be tied to Andorhal’s disturbances in time, but the cause remains unknown.",al={"three oclock watch","andorhal clock frozen","why stopped at 3"}},{q="Why does the Scarlet Crusade attack Andorhal?",a="Scarlet Crusade strike teams try to enter the city and reclaim Lordaeron from the Scourge. The fanatical crusaders send Scarlet Medics, Hunters, and Invokers, but rarely reach the fortified center.",al={"scarlet crusade in andorhal","scarlet patrols andorhal"}}},ang={["class:Paladin"]="As a paladin of the Alliance, you see Andorhal as consecrated ground turned nightmare. The plague poisoned Lordaeron’s grain stores here and doomed the northern kingdom.",["race:Undead"]="As a Forsaken traveler, you may remember the ruined city grimly. Many who walk the Undercity today were citizens of Lordaeron who first swallowed poisoned grain harvested from these fields."},kw={"andorhal","araj the summoner","chromie","grain silos","scourge","temporal parasites","western plaguelands"},rel={"subzone:andorhal","zone:westernplaguelands","topic:scourge"},src={"Ruins of Andorhal"}}
E["subzone:scholomance"] = {t="subzone",n="Scholomance",z="westernplaguelands",s="Beneath Caer Darrow, Scholomance trains mortals and undead in necromancy and the dark arts. Darkmaster Gandling leads the studies, while Ras Frostwhisper watches over the halls.",h="Beneath Caer Darrow, Scholomance trains mortals and undead in necromancy and the dark arts.",sec={{t="A Pact of Ruin",b="Before the Third War, House Barov ruled from Caer Darrow and held vast lands across Lordaeron. Those lands included Brill, Tarren Mill, and Southshore. Fearing the loss of their wealth and mortal lives, the Barovs accepted Kel'Thuzad's promise of eternal life.\n\nThey deeded their fortress and ancestral catacombs to the Cult of the Damned. The cult repaid them by butchering the nobles and turning the crypts into a hidden place to train necromancers.",sp=0},{t="The School of Necromancy",b="Beneath Caer Darrow's haunted ruins, Scholomance has become a center of Scourge industry. In its halls, early strains of the Plague of Undeath were tested on the Barov family's servants. Mortal acolytes now come to master dark magic under Darkmaster Gandling, while Ras Frostwhisper guards the school.\n\nThe Barov family remains as restless undead, trapped in torment.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What is Scholomance?",a="Beneath Caer Darrow, Scholomance trains mortal necromancers, plague researchers, and fleshcrafters. The Cult of the Damned and the Scourge run the secret academy.",al={"what is this place","scholomance lore","explain scholomance"}},{q="Who owns Caer Darrow and the crypts?",a="House Barov once owned Caer Darrow's keep and crypts, along with vast lands across Lordaeron. Seeking immortality, the family surrendered their ancestral home to Kel'Thuzad, who promised them eternal life. The cult butchered the Barovs and raised them as undead thralls within their own halls.",al={"who owned this","house barov","barov family"}},{q="Who runs the academy now?",a="Darkmaster Gandling runs Scholomance as its mortal headmaster, overseeing instruction and torment. The lich Ras Frostwhisper guards the academy on behalf of the Scourge.",al={"who is the boss","who leads scholomance","headmaster"}},{q="What horrors were developed here?",a="The Cult of the Damned tested early strains of the Plague of Undeath at Scholomance. Acolytes learned their craft there as cultists tested the plague on the Barov household servants.",al={"what was made here","experiments in scholomance","abominations"}}},ang={["class:Mage"]="As a Mage, you see Scholomance's lessons as a perversion of arcane scholarship. Magical inquiry has given way to rot, shadow, and unholy desecration.",["race:Undead"]="As Forsaken, you may regard Scholomance with cold familiarity and disgust. Many Scourge methods of enslavement and biological warfare were perfected in its classrooms."},kw={"barov","caer darrow","cult of the damned","darkmaster gandling","kel'thuzad","necromancy","ras frostwhisper","scholomance"},rel={"subzone:caer-darrow","npc:darkmaster-gandling","topic:cult-of-the-damned","topic:scourge","topic:plague-of-undeath","zone:westernplaguelands","npc:eva-sarkhoff","topic:lordaeron"},src={"Scholomance"}}
E["subzone:scholomance-classic"] = {t="subzone",n="Scholomance (Classic)",z="westernplaguelands",s="In the Western Plaguelands, Scholomance trains mortal spellcasters in the Scourge's arts. The academy lies beneath Caer Darrow, hidden in the crypts of the island fortress.",h="In the Western Plaguelands, Scholomance trains mortal spellcasters in the Scourge's arts.",sec={{t="A School in the Tombs",b="Before the Third War laid Lordaeron waste, the rogue archmage Kel'Thuzad sought recruits for his Cult of the Damned. The wealthy Barov family ruled Caer Darrow and became willing benefactors. They traded their lands and crypts for promised immortality. The cult instead slaughtered them and raised them as monstrous undead.\n\nBeneath the ruined fortress, the cult remade the ancient Arathorian catacombs into a school for the dark arts. Mortal acolytes study plaguecraft, soul binding, and flesh shaping beyond watchful eyes. There, they hone the foul magic that shattered Lordaeron.",sp=0},{t="Lich and Headmaster",b="Kel'Thuzad now directs Scourge operations from above, but Scholomance remains active. The eternal lich Ras Frostwhisper watches over the complex in the Scourge's name. The mortal necromancer Darkmaster Gandling leads the school and tutors ambitious sorcerers through horrific experiments.\n\nStudents who show weakness are cast into the catacombs. In the lower vaults, the voracious wight Ravenian lurks, ready to feed on them.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is Scholomance?",a="Scholomance trains mortal spellcasters in the Scourge's dark arts. The secret academy lies deep beneath Caer Darrow, the island fortress.",al={"what is this place","scholomance lore","explain scholomance"}},{q="Who rules Scholomance now?",a="Ras Frostwhisper oversees Scholomance for the Scourge. Darkmaster Gandling directs instruction and mortal affairs as its ruthless headmaster.",al={"who leads scholomance","who is in charge","scholomance boss"}},{q="How did the Scourge acquire Caer Darrow?",a="The noble Barov family gave Caer Darrow and its crypts to the Cult of the Damned after Kel'Thuzad promised them eternal life. The cult answered by slaughtering the Barovs and raising them into undeath.",al={"barov backstory","who owned caer darrow","how did cult get scholomance"}},{q="Why is the school locked?",a="The massive iron gate was sealed to shield the academy's research and summoners from intruders. Opening it requires the Skeleton Key, forged through a complex ritual spanning the Plaguelands.",al={"scholomance door locked","how to get into scholomance","skeleton key scholomance"}}},ang={["class:Mage"]="As a mage, you can see Scholomance twist Dalaran's scholastic traditions into necromancy and decay. It shows what Kirin Tor expertise can become in the service of death.",["class:Paladin"]="As a paladin of the Silver Hand, cleansing the tainted halls beneath Caer Darrow is an urgent duty. Scholomance is a source of the Scourge's mortal leadership."},kw={"barov","caer darrow","cult of the damned","gandling","necromancy","ras frostwhisper","scholomance"},rel={"subzone:caer-darrow","npc:darkmaster-gandling","topic:cult-of-the-damned","topic:plague-of-undeath","topic:scourge","zone:westernplaguelands","subzone:chillwind-camp","subzone:bulwark"},src={"Scholomance (Classic)"}}
E["subzone:sorrow-hill"] = {t="subzone",n="Sorrow Hill",z="westernplaguelands",s="At Sorrow Hill, the dead rise beneath headstones south of Andorhal. Plague cauldrons have corrupted the old burial ground, and its dead roam again.",h="At Sorrow Hill, the dead rise beneath headstones south of Andorhal.",sec={{t="A Burden of Graves",b="Before the Third War, Sorrow Hill received the dead of Andorhal and the nearby townships. When the Scourge brought the Plague of Undeath, the gravediggers could not keep pace. Shallow, poorly marked pits spread around the cemetery’s neat crypts.\n\nTerrified survivors abandoned the old rites and burned their loved ones on a great pyre to the south. They feared the dead would rise. Before Andorhal fell completely, those who remained entombed Lord Uther the Lightbringer on the hill’s high ground. His burial gave the hill its sorrowful name.",sp=0},{t="The Resurrected Dead",b="Plague cauldrons across the region have corrupted Sorrow Hill. Soldiers and citizens buried here now roam among the headstones as skeletal flayers and ravenous ghouls. Skeletal mages and a Scourge commander hold the crypts in the southeast.\n\nThe cemetery lies on the road between Chillwind Camp and Andorhal. The Alliance and the Argent Dawn send patrols to cut down the undead and hold their foothold in the region.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why was this graveyard named Sorrow Hill?",a="Andorhal’s surviving people gave Sorrow Hill its name when they buried Lord Uther the Lightbringer on its high ground. As they fled the Scourge, laying their fallen champion in a grand tomb was their final act together.",al={"sorrow hill name meaning","why is it called sorrow hill"}},{q="Why are there so many shallow graves here?",a="The Plague of Undeath killed people in Andorhal faster than they could build proper tombs. Citizens dug hasty, poorly marked graves, then turned to mass burning when the onslaught overwhelmed them.",al={"shallow graves sorrow hill","why are graves poorly marked"}},{q="Who is buried in Sorrow Hill?",a="Thousands of fallen soldiers and citizens of Andorhal lie at Sorrow Hill, along with Lord Uther the Lightbringer in his great tomb. The cemetery also holds cannoneer Dargal’s resting place and a monument to Joseph Redpath, whose body was destroyed.",al={"famous graves sorrow hill","notable people buried here"}},{q="What threat does Sorrow Hill pose today?",a="The Lich King’s plague cauldrons corrupted Sorrow Hill, and its dead rose as skeletal flayers, ravenous ghouls and skeletal mages. A Scourge commander leads them from the southeastern crypts, threatening the southern approach to Andorhal.",al={"scourge at sorrow hill","who controls sorrow hill"}}},ang={["class:Paladin"]="As a paladin, you find mourning and reverence at Sorrow Hill. Visit Uther’s Tomb and drive back the undead defiling the grounds around your mentor.",["faction:Alliance"]="Just down the road from Chillwind Camp, Sorrow Hill guards the way to Andorhal. It is also the sacred resting place of Lordaeron’s fallen defenders."},kw={"andorhal cemetery","dargal","joseph redpath","skeletal flayers","sorrow hill","uther's tomb","western plaguelands"},rel={"subzone:uther-s-tomb","subzone:andorhal","subzone:chillwind-camp","zone:westernplaguelands","topic:plague-of-undeath","subzone:cauldron","topic:argent-dawn","topic:scourge"},src={"Sorrow Hill"}}
E["subzone:uther-s-tomb"] = {t="subzone",n="Uther's Tomb",z="westernplaguelands",s="On Sorrow Hill in the Western Plaguelands, Uther's Tomb remains untouched by the blight. His followers raised it after Arthas slew him near Andorhal.",h="On Sorrow Hill in the Western Plaguelands, Uther's Tomb remains untouched by the blight.",sec={{t="A Bastion in the Blight",b="South of Andorhal's ruins, Uther's Tomb marks the resting place of Uther, who founded the Knights of the Silver Hand. After Lordaeron fell, he made his last stand in Andorhal. There he defended King Terenas Menethil II's urn of ashes from Prince Arthas Menethil and the Scourge.\n\nArthas killed his former mentor and took the urn to carry Kel'Thuzad's remains. Surviving soldiers recovered Uther's body and laid him in a stone sanctuary. Though the surrounding land is corrupted, the tomb remains untouched by decay under High Priest Thel'danis's watch.",sp=0},{t="The Lightbringer's Legacy",b="The Path of Uther leads to a grand stone effigy of the paladin. A tome of the Holy Light rests in one hand, and his warhammer in the other. Pilgrims brave these roads to pay homage, pray, or reflect on the devotion that shaped the first paladins.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is buried in this tomb?",a="Uther the Lightbringer rests here. He founded and commanded the Knights of the Silver Hand, the first paladin order in human history. Before Lordaeron fell to the Scourge, he mentored Prince Arthas Menethil.",al={"who is uther","who is buried here","uther the lightbringer"}},{q="How did Uther die?",a="Uther fell in Andorhal, slain by his former student, Arthas Menethil. Arthas had returned from Northrend as a death knight. Uther died defending the urn that held the ashes of Arthas's father, King Terenas Menethil II.",al={"who killed uther","how did uther die","arthas kills uther"}},{q="Who is High Priest Thel'danis?",a="High Priest Thel'danis cares for the monument and keeps a quiet, sacred vigil over Uther's resting place. He braves the surrounding undead to keep the shrine a sanctuary of the Light.",al={"theldanis","priest at uther's tomb","who protects the tomb"}},{q="Why isn't the tomb corrupted by the plague?",a="Uther's memory and the enduring power of the Holy Light consecrate the grounds. Sorrow Hill's surrounding forests have withered and rotted, while the shrine remains an unbroken sanctuary against the blight.",al={"why is uther's tomb clean","why no plague at tomb"}}},ang={["class:Paladin"]="As a paladin, standing before Uther's statue honors the father of the order. His sacrifice embodies the virtues of the Silver Hand.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance traveler, this tomb recalls Lordaeron's fallen legacy. It offers a place for quiet reflection amid the horrors of the Plaguelands."},kw={"andorhal","arthas","lightbringer","silver hand","sorrow hill","theldanis","uther"},rel={"subzone:sorrow-hill","subzone:ruins-of-andorhal","topic:knights-of-the-silver-hand","topic:arthas-menethil","topic:terenas-menethil-ii","topic:light","zone:westernplaguelands"},src={"Uther's Tomb"}}
E["subzone:weeping-cave"] = {t="subzone",n="Weeping Cave",z="westernplaguelands",s="Toxic blight seeps through Weeping Cave in the northeastern hills of the Western Plaguelands, just west of the Thondroril River. Grotesque fungal beasts and oozes shelter in its tunnels.",h="Toxic blight seeps through Weeping Cave in the northeastern hills of the Western Plaguelands, just west of...",sec={{t="A Den of Rot",b="Above the Thondroril River, moisture trickles through Weeping Cave’s rocky ceiling. The Scourge’s plague has poisoned the soil overhead, and foul runoff drains into the dark tunnels. Rotting horrors and decaying behemoths roam there with caustic oozes. A corrupted elemental called The Husk dwells in the cave as well.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where is the Weeping Cave located?",a="Weeping Cave lies in the northeastern hills of the Western Plaguelands, just west of the Thondroril River near the Eastern Plaguelands border.",al={"weeping cave location","where is weeping cave","find weeping cave"}},{q="What creatures dwell inside the cave?",a="Rotting behemoths, decaying horrors, toxic creeping slimes, and a rare elemental called The Husk dwell inside Weeping Cave.",al={"weeping cave monsters","what is inside weeping cave","weeping cave mobs"}},{q="Why is it called the Weeping Cave?",a="Moisture drips continually from the cave’s ceiling, making the stone seem to weep. Plague has turned the runoff rancid, and it fosters virulent fungal growth.",al={"why is it called weeping cave","weeping cave name meaning"}},{q="Who is The Husk?",a="The Husk is a rare corrupted elemental deep within Weeping Cave. Lingering alchemical blight in the surrounding earth and water has warped it.",al={"the husk","the husk weeping cave","husk rare"}}},ang={["class:Druid"]="As a druid, you see nature turned against itself in Weeping Cave. The plague of undeath has corrupted its subterranean flora and elemental energies into violent monstrosities."},kw={"decaying horror","ooze","rotting behemoth","the husk","thondroril river","weeping cave","western plaguelands"},rel={"zone:westernplaguelands","subzone:thondroril-river"},src={"Weeping Cave"}}
E["subzone:writhing-haunt"] = {t="subzone",n="Writhing Haunt",z="westernplaguelands",s="East of the Ruins of Andorhal, plague vapors drift from the Writhing Haunt across the Western Plaguelands. The Scourge seized this farmstead, once fertile land that fed Lordaeron, and turned it into a source of disease.",h="East of the Ruins of Andorhal, plague vapors drift from the Writhing Haunt across the Western Plaguelands.",sec={{t="A Field of Disease",b="During the Third War, the Writhing Haunt fell swiftly, like many human homesteads around Andorhal. Its fields now yield rot instead of crops. The Scourge planted an enormous plague cauldron in the tilled earth, where it continually vents diseased vapors. Rotting ghouls, freezing ghouls, and fetid zombies wander the overgrown furrows. Cauldron Lord Razarch commands them and guards the machinery.",sp=0},{t="A Watcher in the Ruins",b="The cauldron's choking miasma has not driven everyone away. Mulgris Deepriver, a tauren druid, lingers inside one of the dilapidated farmhouses. He came to heal nature's wounds, but the plague has stricken him too. Unable to cure the suffering beasts, he asks capable travelers to grant the diseased wolves and other wildlife a swift, merciful release.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What was the Writhing Haunt before the plague?",a="Before the Third War, the Writhing Haunt was a productive human farm. It sustained the land and supplied grain and livestock to nearby Andorhal and the greater Kingdom of Lordaeron.",al={"writhing haunt history","what was this farm","old farm andorhal"}},{q="Why is there a giant cauldron in the middle of the field?",a="The Scourge placed the giant cauldron in the field to brew and spread plague vapors across the countryside. The vapors poison soil, water, and nearby living creatures.",al={"plague cauldron writhing haunt","why cauldron here","green smoke farm"}},{q="Who controls the Writhing Haunt?",a="Cauldron Lord Razarch, an undead servant of the Scourge, commands the site. Ghouls and zombies guard the plague cauldron for him.",al={"who is in charge writhing haunt","writhing haunt boss","razarch"}},{q="Who is hiding in the farmhouse?",a="Mulgris Deepriver, a tauren druid, shelters inside an abandoned farmhouse. He came to the Plaguelands to heal nature, but the plague cannot be cured, so he asks travelers to end the suffering of diseased wildlife.",al={"npc in house","mulgris deepriver","who is mulgris"}}},ang={["class:Druid"]="Plague vapors desecrate the Writhing Haunt's rich farmland and offend the natural order. The cauldron must be silenced.",["faction:Alliance"]="The farmland outside Andorhal lies under Scourge rule, reduced to a diseased wasteland. It is a bitter reminder of Lordaeron's fall."},kw={"andorhal","cauldron lord razarch","mulgris deepriver","plague cauldron","western plaguelands","writhing haunt"},rel={"zone:westernplaguelands","subzone:ruins-of-andorhal","topic:scourge","subzone:cauldron","subzone:andorhal"},src={"Writhing Haunt"}}
E["zone:westernplaguelands"] = {t="zone",n="Western Plaguelands",z="westernplaguelands",s="Toxic mist and undead legions choke the Western Plaguelands, where rival factions fight for ground. Once northern Lordaeron’s breadbasket, its farms and towns fell to Kel'Thuzad’s cauldrons, though life still clings to the soil. The Argent Dawn, Alliance, Forsaken, and Scarlet Crusade wage desperate campaigns across its blighted fields.",h="Toxic mist and undead legions choke the Western Plaguelands, where rival factions fight for ground.",sec={{t="The Breadbasket of Lordaeron",b="Before the Third War, farms spread east from Tirisfal Glades toward Darrowmere Lake. Hearthglen governed the north from Mardenholde Keep, while Andorhal stored and shipped grain across the kingdom. So Kel'Thuzad made the region his primary target. At Andorhal, the Cult of the Damned put the Plague of Undeath into grain shipments, turning Lordaeron's food supply into its doom.",sp=0},{t="A Land Under Siege",b="The Scourge raised four great plague cauldrons to poison the soil. They stand at Felstone Field, Dalson's Tears, the Writhing Haunt, and Gahrron's Withering. Monstrous Cauldron Lords tend the vats and fill the air with toxic fog. Trees twist with swollen growths, and blighted wildlife rampages through the brush. Beneath Caer Darrow on Darrowmere Lake, Darkmaster Gandling trains necromancers at Scholomance, adding to the undead threat.",sp=0},{t="Divided Factions",b="The Scourge holds much of the region, yet other factions keep footholds. In the north, the Scarlet Crusade controls Hearthglen and purges whatever it deems tainted. Alliance forces gather at Chillwind Camp in the south, while the Forsaken defend their borders from the Bulwark. The neutral Argent Dawn directs the fight against the cauldrons, aids champions of both factions, and guards Uther's Tomb, the region's last truly sanctified ground.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why did the Plague hit this area so hard?",a="Andorhal shipped grain across northern Lordaeron, making it a target for Kel'Thuzad. The Cult of the Damned put the Plague of Undeath into grain shipments there, then raised plague cauldrons at four major farmsteads to spread undeath through the kingdom's food supply.",al={"why is western plaguelands plagued","what happened to andorhal","why cauldrons here"}},{q="Who controls Hearthglen in the north?",a="The Scarlet Crusade controls Hearthglen and Mardenholde Keep. Once a regional administrative hub for Lordaeron, the fortress is now held by zealots who execute outsiders approaching their borders and distrust all non-crusaders.",al={"hearthglen faction","who lives in mardenholde keep","is hearthglen friendly"}},{q="Where can Alliance and Horde players find safe outposts?",a="The Alliance gathers at Chillwind Camp near the southern border with the Alterac Mountains, where it has a flight master and Argent Dawn allies. The Horde operates from the Bulwark on the western border, reached from Tirisfal Glades.",al={"where are the flight paths","horde camp wpl","alliance camp wpl"}},{q="What is the purpose of the plague cauldrons in the fields?",a="The Cult of the Damned raised plague cauldrons at Felstone Field, Dalson's Tears, the Writhing Haunt, and Gahrron's Withering. They pump plague vapors into the air and soil. Argent Dawn agents recruit adventurers to slay the Cauldron Lords and counter-engineer the toxic brews.",al={"what are the cauldrons","cauldron purpose","felstone cauldron"}},{q="What is Scholomance and where is it located?",a="Scholomance is a subterranean academy of necromancy run by the Scourge and the Cult of the Damned. It lies beneath the ruins of Caer Darrow, an island fortress in the southeastern waters of Darrowmere Lake.",al={"scholomance location","where is scholomance","caer darrow dungeon"}},{q="Is any part of the Western Plaguelands uncorrupted?",a="Uther's Tomb on Sorrow Hill, near the zone's southern edge, remains holy and untouched by blight. It is a consecrated memorial to High General Uther the Lightbringer and the lost Order of the Silver Hand.",al={"holy ground in wpl","is uther tomb clean","uther's tomb safe"}}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="Chillwind Camp is the Alliance's forward garrison. Commander Ashlam Valorfist directs campaigns from there to disrupt the plague cauldrons and avenge Lordaeron's fallen cities.",["faction:Horde"]="The Bulwark marks the frontier of Forsaken sovereignty. From there, the Horde pushes east to neutralize Scourge commanders and challenge Scarlet zealots along their vulnerable flank.",["class:Paladin"]="As a paladin, you face a solemn trial in Lordaeron's desecrated fields. You can make pilgrimage to Uther's Tomb and fight the horrors of Scholomance and Hearthglen's corrupted zealots.",["profession:Herbalism"]="As a herbalist, you can find rare and dangerous plants such as Plaguebloom and Arthas' Tears rooted among blighted pine groves, where lingering taint lets them grow."},kw={"andorhal","bulwark","caer darrow","cauldrons","chillwind camp","hearthglen","mardenholde keep","scholomance","uther's tomb","western plaguelands"},rel={"zone:easternplaguelands","subzone:ruins-of-andorhal","subzone:scholomance","subzone:hearthglen","subzone:uther-s-tomb","subzone:bulwark","subzone:chillwind-camp","topic:scourge"},src={"Western Plaguelands (Classic)","Western Plaguelands"}}
